          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            geometry of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            close to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizon"} horizon
            is called its
            = succeed "." do
              %em near-horizon geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %em far-horizon geometry
            %em interpolates
            between its near and far horizon geometry.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            In the following “small” and “large”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
            is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/units"} units
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_P
            times a root of the integer charge (“number”
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi P
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi N
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≪
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac
                  { r }
                  {
                  \\ell_P \, N^{1/k}
                  }
                  \\;\ll\; 1
          %p while “far” from the horizon means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi P
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi N
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≫
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac
                  { r }
                  {  \ell_P \,  N^{1/k} }
                  \\;\gg\;
                  1
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AFFHS98"} AFFHS 98, (2), (7) and below (11)
          %p
            This means that the near/far horizon limit may also be thought of as corresponding to large/small
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
            “is tiny” and due to the higher roots of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            appearing here, this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            must be “huge” for the near horizon limit to be visible at macroscopic scale, while, conversely, any “moderate” value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            means implies that every macroscopic radius is “far” from the horizon.
          %h3#NearHorizonGeometry Near-horizon geometry
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            that preserve some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_{p+2}
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein manifold
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mn 11
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{11-(p+2)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ads
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ads_{p+2} \times X_{d-(p+2)}
                  \\,;
          %p
            while for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            the near horizon geometry is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformation"} conformal
            to a geometry of this form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_{p+2} \times X_{d-(p+2)}
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AFFHS98"} AFFHS 98, section 2
          %h3#FarHorizonGeometry Far-horizon geometry
          %p
            In contrast, the “far-horizon geometry” of all those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            whose near horizon geometry is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_{p+2} \times X_{d-(p+2)}
            (i.e. actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
            without conformal factor) is of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{p,1} \times C\left(X_{d-(p+2)}\right)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (the brane
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X_{d-(p+2)})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+cone"} metric cone
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{d-(p+2)}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AFFHS98"} AFFHS 98, section 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            away from the tip of the cone, it may in itself be regarded as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone+brane"}> cone brane
            ”-solution (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AFFHS98"} AFFHS 98, section 3.1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{d-(p+2)}
            is a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone+brane"} cone brane
            is a brane “at an
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
          %p
            Examples and applications of such
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone+branes"} cone branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+space+holography"} flat space holography
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
            The near/far horizon limits of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#BlackM2"} The black M2-brane
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#BlackM5Brane"} The black M5-brane
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#MK6Brane"} The MK6-brane
          %h3#BlackM2 The black M2-brane
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            is given (we follow
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AFFHS98"} AFFHS98, §2.1.1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
          #eq:BlackM2BraneMetric.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{M2} \;\coloneqq\;
                  H^{- 2/3} g_{(\mathbb{R}^{2,1})}
                  +
                  H^{1/3} g_{C(X_7)}
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} strength
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi dvol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_{M2}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  dvol_{\mathbb{R}^{2,1}} \wedge d H^{-1}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X_7)
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+cone"} metric cone
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            7-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_7
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda = 5
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{C(X)}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  (d r)^2 + r^2 g_{X_7}
                  \\,,
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi th
                        %mn 6
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi th
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 6
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 6
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 6
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H \;\coloneqq\; 1 + \frac{\ell_{th}^6}{r^6}
                  \\:,
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\ell_{th} \;\coloneqq\; 2^{5/6} \pi^{2/6} N^{1/6} \ell_P
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            and with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_P
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
            in 11 dimensions.
          %p
            In the near-horizon/large
            = succeed "-limit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi th
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_{th} \to \infty
            this becomes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi M
                              %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ℓ
                                %mi th
                              %mo ≫
                              %mn 1
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %msub
                                %mi ℓ
                                %mi th
                              %mo )
                            %mn 4
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 2
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %msub
                                %mi ℓ
                                %mi th
                              %mo )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 7
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %msub
                                %mi ℓ
                                %mi th
                              %mo )
                            %mn 4
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
