          %h3#MK6Brane The MK6-brane
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+tensor"} metric tensor
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopoles"} KK-monopoles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            in the limit that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi th
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_{th} \coloneqq N \ell_P \to 0
            is
          #eq:SmallNMK6.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi MK
                      %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sin
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi φ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi cos
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi ϕ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{MK6}
                  \\;=\;
                  g_{\mathbb{R}^{6,1}}
                  +
                  (d y)^2
                  +
                  y^2
                  \\big(
                  (d \theta)^2
                  +
                  (\sin \theta)^2 (d \varphi)^2
                  +
                  (\cos \theta)^2 (d \phi)^2
                  \\big)
          %p subject to the identification
          #eq:OrbifoldIdentificationForKKMonopole.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∼
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\varphi, \phi)
                  \\;\sim\;
                  (\varphi, \phi) + (2\pi/N ,2\pi/N)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is equation (47) in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#IMSY98"} IMSY 98
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi g
                          %mi YM
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 3
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 3
                        %msub
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mi P
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≫
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U/\left(\frac{N}{g^{2/3}_{YM}}\right)
                  \\;=\;
                  U/\left(\frac{N}{(2\pi)^{4/3} \ell_P}\right)
                  \\;\gg\;
                  1
          %p
            from a few lines above. Inserting this condition into the definition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 2
                  %mi N
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y^2 \coloneqq 2 N \ell^3_P U
            right above (47) shows that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi y
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %mi N
