                  y^2
                  \&amp; =
                  2 N \ell^3_P U
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  2(2\pi)^{-4/3} N^2 \ell_P^2
                  \\;
                  \\underset{
                  \\gg 1
                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\left(U/\left(\frac{N}{ (2 \pi)^{4/3} \ell_P}\right)\right)
                  }}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            hence that the distance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            from the locus of the MK6-brane is large in units of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
